    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The given determinant is \\(\\det \\mathbf{M} = -2\\). We are asked to find \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4)\\). \n\nFirst, recall a key property of determinants. Specifically, for any square matrix \\(\\mathbf{A}\\), the determinant of the matrix raised to a power is given by \\(\\det(\\mathbf{A}^k) = (\\det \\mathbf{A})^k\\). In this case, we need to find \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4)\\).\n\nGiven that \\(\\det \\mathbf{M} = -2\\), we can substitute this value into the property mentioned above:\n\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (\\det \\mathbf{M})^4\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute the given value of \\(\\det \\mathbf{M}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (-2)^4\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\((-2)^4\\):\n\n\\[\n(-2)^4 = (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) = 16\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the determinant of \\(\\mathbf{M}^4\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]",
